# Personal Command Center Dashboard

A personal command-center web app that unifies astrophotography planning, calendar, tasks, and AI into one fast homepage, designed to run on a dedicated always-on server and be accessed from any device via Tailscale.

## Summary

A personal command-center web app that unifies astrophotography planning, calendar, tasks, and AI into one fast homepage, designed to run on a dedicated always-on server and be accessed from any device via Tailscale.

## Context: What You Already Have

This dashboard is NOT built from scratch. It ties together existing projects:

- **PersonalWebsite** (`~/PycharmProjects/PersonalWebsite`) — Next.js 16 / React 19 / Tailwind 4 / next-auth. Already has an `/admin` route with Google OAuth and an `/astrophotography` gallery driven by `src/data/dsoData.ts` (structured DSO entries with title, date, type, constellation, telescope, exposure, location, catalogues). This is the stack template to copy.
- **LocalImageTool / Photo-AI** (`Gonhog-Creator/LocalImageTool`, private) — Self-hosted local AI photo/video indexer. Targets Windows + RTX 4070 + Docker + Immich. Has idempotent scanning, stage-based processing state, read-only media mounts. Roadmap already plans a "public website export mode" that produces static metadata for PersonalWebsite. THIS is the photo server for the always-on PC.
- **SeeStar-AstroStat-2.0** (`Gonhog-Creator/SeeStar-AstroStat-2.0`, public fork) — PowerShell utility that recursively scans `.fit`/`.fits` files, groups by object/session, calculates total frames + exposure time + storage size. The exact logic the dashboard's FITS scanner needs (to be ported to TS/Python).
- **SecondBrain** (`~/PycharmProjects/SecondBrain`) — Obsidian-based knowledge base with an AI-maintained wiki (CASCADE.md schema). Could be surfaced inside the dashboard later.
- **Other repos**: DeltaDash, EvolutionSim, RoADashboard, SplatStudio, DeltaVOdooMiddleware, DeltaVision, BudgetTool, TauEncoder, GaussianTool.

## Key Decisions (from Q&A)

| Decision | Choice | Implication |
|---|---|---|
| Deployment | **Server + thin clients** via Tailscale | State lives on the dedicated always-on PC. MacBook/PC/phone are just browsers. Works even when MacBook is off. |
| Project structure | **New separate repo** (`Dashboard`) | Keeps public website separate from private command center. Different security, different deploy. |
| Astro data | **API-driven + FITS scan** | Weather API for conditions; scan FITS headers to detect what you imaged. No manual target logging. |
| Website sync | **Defer** (flag-only for now) | Dashboard lists "final images not yet on website". Auto-publish + agent commit comes later. |
| Calendar | **Google + Apple** | Google via OAuth API; Apple via local CalDAV / Calendar.app data on the server. |
| Auth | **Tailscale + (TBD)** | Tailscale is the primary boundary. A lightweight login may be added since you want access from any device/network, not just Tailnet. |
| AI layer | **Both chat + scheduled jobs** | Context-aware chat (knows your todos/calendar/astro) AND scheduled background AI reports. |
| OpenAI automations | **Plan for both** | Dashboard can run its own scheduled AI jobs AND ingest reports from external automations. |
| Background work | **Cron now, agent loops later** | MVP = a jobs panel with scheduled scripts/HTTP calls. Long-running agent loops plug in later as another job type. |
| Local LLM | **Defer** | Use OpenAI now. Ollama/local model support added later once you decide on multi-agent orchestration. |
| MVP slice | **Skeleton + astro planner + calendar/tasks** | Deliver the shell, the astro planner end-to-end, AND the calendar+tasks. AI layer is phase 2. |
| Layout | **Fixed CSS grid** (MVP) | No drag-drop lib yet; SSR-safe and fast. Revisit react-grid-layout in Phase 2/3. |
| Theme | **Dark-first** | True greys, elevation via lightness steps, one accent. tweakcn-generated palette. Light mode later. |
| Space news | **Deferred** | Daily AI report widget designed (see dashboard-research.md §7) but not in MVP build — user will figure out the ChatGPT connection later. `Report` table + ingest endpoint design preserved for when it's picked up. |

