**Why this shape:**
- The server is the single source of truth. If your MacBook is off, the dashboard still runs, jobs still fire, FITS still get scanned.
- Thin clients = zero install on MacBook/phone. Just a URL.
- Tailscale gives you HTTPS + auth + access from any network, not just home.
- Photo-AI already lives on this PC and already indexes the FITS — the dashboard just queries it rather than duplicating that work.

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Framework | **Next.js 16** (App Router) | Matches PersonalWebsite — familiar, server actions + API routes give FS access |
| UI | **React 19 + Tailwind 4 + shadcn/ui** | Matches PersonalWebsite; shadcn for fast dashboard widgets |
| Language | **TypeScript** | Matches PersonalWebsite |
| Database | **SQLite via Prisma** | Single-file, lives on server, no DB server to run, easy backup. Good enough for one user. |
| Auth | **next-auth (Google OAuth)** + Tailscale boundary | Reuse PersonalWebsite's pattern. Tailscale gates network access. |
| Scheduler | **node-cron** (in-process) | Simplest possible. Jobs run inside the Next server. Phase 2 can swap for a real queue. |
| Weather API | **Open-Meteo** (free, no key) | Cloud cover, transparency, seeing forecasts. Free tier is generous. |
| Astro targets | **astronomy-engine** (npm) | Pure JS, no deps. Computes object positions/visibility from lat/lon/time. |
| FITS parsing | **`fitsjs` / `astrofits` / port SeeStar logic to TS** | Read FITS headers (OBJECT, DATE-OBS, EXPTIME, IMAGETYP) in Node |
| Calendar | **Google Calendar API** + **node-caldav-client** (Apple) | Google via OAuth (reuse next-auth google). Apple via CalDAV to iCloud. |
| AI (phase 2) | **OpenAI SDK** behind a provider interface | Provider interface lets Ollama swap in later without touching call sites. |
| Deployment | **PM2** or **`next start`** as a Windows service | Keeps it running 24/7 on the server. Tailscale Serve exposes it as HTTPS. |

## MVP Scope (Phase 1)

The MVP delivers three things, all running on the server:

### 1. Dashboard Shell
- Single-page layout with a sidebar / top nav of widgets
- Set as browser homepage; loads fast (SSR, minimal JS)
- Sections: Astro Planner, Calendar, Tasks, System (later), Jobs (later)
- Reuse PersonalWebsite's next-auth Google login + Tailwind theme

### 2. Astrophotography Planner (the headline feature)
- **Tonight panel**: cloud cover, transparency, seeing, moon phase for your location (Bald Head Island, NC per your dsoData) via Open-Meteo
- **Target suggestions**: list of DSOs visible tonight from your lat/lon, sorted by altitude/transit time, using astronomy-engine + a built-in target catalog (start with the Messier + your existing dsoData entries)
- **FITS scan**: recursively scan a configurable path (e.g. `D:\Astrophotography`), parse FITS headers, group by OBJECT + session, show total frames/exposure per target. Port SeeStar-AstroStat logic to TS.
- **"Needs update" list**: compares FITS-scanned final images against what's published in PersonalWebsite's `dsoData.ts` and flags targets you've imaged but not yet published. (Flag only — no auto-publish in MVP.)
- **Astro todo list**: a dedicated task list for astro prep (e.g. "charge battery", "polar align", "update target list")

### 3. Calendar + Tasks
- **Unified calendar**: merge Google Calendar (OAuth) + Apple Calendar (CalDAV to iCloud) into one agenda view
- **Task manager**: todos with projects, due dates, priorities. Stored in SQLite. Replaces whatever you use now.
- **Today view**: the homepage shows today's events + due tasks + tonight's astro conditions in one glance

